WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:01.567 --> 00:00:03.035
-Now that I have everyone's
attention,

00:00:03.035 --> 00:00:04.603
I would like to introduce
the 2022 mayor's

00:00:04.603 --> 00:00:06.739
youth leadership program
participants.

00:00:06.739 --> 00:00:10.777
And in the interest of
inclusion, partici-skirts.

00:00:10.777 --> 00:00:14.647
Ines Herrera was a finalist
in the intel space competition.

00:00:14.647 --> 00:00:17.116
She speaks Spanish and Mandarin.

00:00:17.116 --> 00:00:18.684
Oh, gosh, it doesn't say English
here.

00:00:18.684 --> 00:00:23.956
So wel-come, In-es.

00:00:23.956 --> 00:00:27.192
-Welcome back to "Late Night."
We're here with Tina Fey.

00:00:27.192 --> 00:00:29.795
That was a clip
from "Mr. Mayor."

00:00:29.795 --> 00:00:32.098
-Yes.
-Dream cast.

00:00:32.098 --> 00:00:33.466
Ted Danson.
-Yes.

00:00:33.466 --> 00:00:35.201
-Holly Hunter. And then
our friend Bobby Moynihan.

00:00:35.201 --> 00:00:36.169
-Bobby Moynihan.
-Yeah.

00:00:36.169 --> 00:00:37.903
-Vella Lovell and Mike Cabellon.

00:00:37.903 --> 00:00:39.371
And they are so, so funny.

00:00:39.371 --> 00:00:43.142
Yeah, it's so fun to get to work
with Bobby again

00:00:43.142 --> 00:00:45.445
'cause we didn't overlap
all that much, me and Bobby.

00:00:45.445 --> 00:00:46.813
-Yeah.
-Or maybe at all.

00:00:46.813 --> 00:00:49.148
I don't remember.
-He might have been there right,

00:00:49.148 --> 00:00:50.916
like, probably that 2008 year

00:00:50.916 --> 00:00:52.652
when you were coming back
for Sarah Palin.

00:00:52.652 --> 00:00:56.122
-So much of my late time when I
was there was such a blur,

00:00:56.122 --> 00:00:57.423
that I, like --
Sometimes I'm like,

00:00:57.423 --> 00:00:58.892
"Mulaney's not Jost, right?"

00:00:58.892 --> 00:01:00.493
[ Laughter ]

00:01:00.493 --> 00:01:03.363
-A lot of people
have that problem. Yeah.

00:01:03.363 --> 00:01:06.031
[ Laughter ]

00:01:06.031 --> 00:01:09.001
-But, yeah, and Ted Danson
and Holly Hunter.

00:01:09.001 --> 00:01:11.537
And, like, sometimes Ted Danson
will call me, and I still, like,

00:01:11.537 --> 00:01:13.473
my phone will say, like, it'll
say "Ted Danson."

00:01:13.473 --> 00:01:14.707
And I'm like --
[ Laughs ]

00:01:14.707 --> 00:01:15.908
"That's crazy."
[ Laughter ]

00:01:15.908 --> 00:01:17.610
"That's crazy."
-Yeah.

00:01:17.610 --> 00:01:19.845
I mean, I would say both Ted
and Holly are the kind of people

00:01:19.845 --> 00:01:23.950
that if you came up with any
sort of respect or curiosity

00:01:23.950 --> 00:01:25.985
about comedy, they're just two
people that you're just thr--

00:01:25.985 --> 00:01:27.353
you can't believe you get to
talk to them.

00:01:27.353 --> 00:01:28.554
-Yes. You can't believe you get
to talk to them,

00:01:28.554 --> 00:01:30.890
and you spend a lot of energy,
like, making sure

00:01:30.890 --> 00:01:33.192
you don't say like,
"I want a toddler, hi."

00:01:33.192 --> 00:01:35.194
Like, you can't -- you have to,
like, not do their catch phrases

00:01:35.194 --> 00:01:37.196
to them or things
you love about them.

00:01:37.196 --> 00:01:41.934
That show, we monitored, because
of the endless pandemic,

00:01:41.934 --> 00:01:43.802
they would be filming in
California, and I would monitor

00:01:43.802 --> 00:01:46.439
the set from home,
so it would be, like, later.

00:01:46.439 --> 00:01:48.741
It'd be like, 7:00 at night
or I'd be cleaning up dinner,

00:01:48.741 --> 00:01:51.043
and I'd have a little computer
with a Zoom open.

00:01:51.043 --> 00:01:53.246
I could see the set on my TV,
and then the Zoom was

00:01:53.246 --> 00:01:54.513
if the actors
wanted to talk to me.

00:01:54.513 --> 00:01:55.981
So sometimes, Holly Hunter
would just be like,

00:01:55.981 --> 00:01:58.084
"You got anything for me?"
And I'm like, "Oh, God!

00:01:58.084 --> 00:02:02.789
Uh, yes. I think -- I think
the one where you're really --"

00:02:02.789 --> 00:02:04.556
And I'd just be, like, making --

00:02:04.556 --> 00:02:06.826
And she knew I was
making stuff up.

00:02:06.826 --> 00:02:09.462
-You also have "Girls5eva."
-Yes.

00:02:09.462 --> 00:02:10.829
-This is about
to come out again,

00:02:10.829 --> 00:02:12.599
season two on Peacock.
-Yeah, season 2 of "Girls5eva"

00:02:12.599 --> 00:02:14.400
comes out -- you can remember it
very easily --

00:02:14.400 --> 00:02:16.201
It's May 5th.
It's "Girls5eva" on 5/5.

00:02:16.201 --> 00:02:17.803
-Oh, perfect. Oh, look at that.

00:02:17.803 --> 00:02:19.739
-Classy.
-Very nicely done.

00:02:19.739 --> 00:02:23.409
-Yes, on Peacock.

00:02:23.409 --> 00:02:25.711
My friend, Andrea Martin --
you guys know --

00:02:25.711 --> 00:02:27.246
-Yeah, of course.
-She wanted to watch

00:02:27.246 --> 00:02:29.515
"Girls5eva,"
and so I went to her house

00:02:29.515 --> 00:02:32.418
and for like two hours,
I got Peacock on her TV.

00:02:32.418 --> 00:02:34.587
And I'm willing to do that
for anybody that needs it.

00:02:34.587 --> 00:02:36.489
[ Laughter ]

00:02:36.489 --> 00:02:38.658
And then she loved it. Anyway.

00:02:38.658 --> 00:02:40.960
So, yeah, that comes out,
starring Paula Pell,

00:02:40.960 --> 00:02:44.530
Sara Bareilles, Busy Philipps,
Renee Elise Goldsberry,

00:02:44.530 --> 00:02:47.600
guest stars Andrew Rannells,
guest star Amber Ruffin.

00:02:47.600 --> 00:02:49.635
-Amber Ruffin, who was just
right here next to me.

00:02:49.635 --> 00:02:51.737
-Mm-hmm.
-John Lutz, of both of this show

00:02:51.737 --> 00:02:53.205
and "30 Rock" and "SNL" fame.

00:02:53.205 --> 00:02:55.308
-Yes, John Lutz and Paula Pell
are reunited,

00:02:55.308 --> 00:02:57.510
if you guys were fans of
"The Mapleworth Murders."

00:02:57.510 --> 00:03:00.012
-Yeah.
-And you should be.

00:03:00.012 --> 00:03:01.280
-Speaking of murders,

00:03:01.280 --> 00:03:02.815
you got to be in
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:03:02.815 --> 00:03:04.016
-Yes.
-By the way,

00:03:04.016 --> 00:03:05.384
"speaking of murders"
was a terrible segue.

00:03:05.384 --> 00:03:06.819
-"Speaking of murders,
I'm going to kill you."

00:03:06.819 --> 00:03:08.421
-Speaking ever murders, I think
you have something to tell

00:03:08.421 --> 00:03:10.856
everybody about
the Bayside Strangler.

00:03:10.856 --> 00:03:12.025
-Crickets.

00:03:12.025 --> 00:03:14.961
[ Laughter ]

00:03:14.961 --> 00:03:18.063
-So, you got to work -- Now,
obviously, over the years,

00:03:18.063 --> 00:03:19.265
you've gotten to hang out,

00:03:19.265 --> 00:03:21.667
work with Steve Martin
and Martin Short.

00:03:21.667 --> 00:03:24.137
But being with them at the same
time just must be --

00:03:24.137 --> 00:03:26.472
-Honestly, it's, like, one of
the greatest joys of my life

00:03:26.472 --> 00:03:29.842
that I've gotten to meet those
guys and to have a small part on

00:03:29.842 --> 00:03:32.111
"Only Murders in the Building,"
a show that my whole family

00:03:32.111 --> 00:03:33.946
enjoys and is very invested in.

00:03:33.946 --> 00:03:35.882
And it's just --
It is the most joyful set

00:03:35.882 --> 00:03:37.650
because those guys love
each other.

00:03:37.650 --> 00:03:40.085
-They really do.
-They love each other so much.

00:03:40.085 --> 00:03:42.121
It's the happiest set.

00:03:42.121 --> 00:03:44.389
Also, it's fun to do a murder
mystery thing because you just

00:03:44.389 --> 00:03:48.527
kind of get your pages,
and sometimes you don't know

00:03:48.527 --> 00:03:51.831
what's happening, and you don't
have any context

00:03:51.831 --> 00:03:53.265
for why your character
is doing that.

00:03:53.265 --> 00:03:55.868
And for me, that doesn't change
my acting at all.

00:03:55.868 --> 00:03:57.303
-Right.
-So that's like, "Sure!"

00:03:57.303 --> 00:03:58.971
-You've never cared about
the backstory of your character.

00:03:58.971 --> 00:04:01.240
-No, no.

00:04:01.240 --> 00:04:03.676
-You know, it's funny, because
we've obviously done

00:04:03.676 --> 00:04:06.345
charity events, the same kind
of events that those guys do.

00:04:06.345 --> 00:04:08.881
And the amazing thing about
Marty and Steve is

00:04:08.881 --> 00:04:11.184
how seriously they take
being silly.

00:04:11.184 --> 00:04:12.485
-Yes.
-And, like, when you see them

00:04:12.485 --> 00:04:15.254
backstage before they go on,
they're writing jokes.

00:04:15.254 --> 00:04:17.556
They're constantly
tightening the screws.

00:04:17.556 --> 00:04:19.892
And how much they care about
the minutia of comedy, I think,

00:04:19.892 --> 00:04:21.928
speaks to the longevity of
what they've been doing.

00:04:21.928 --> 00:04:24.330
-For sure.
They love, probably, rehearsing

00:04:24.330 --> 00:04:25.731
as much as they love
doing stuff.

00:04:25.731 --> 00:04:27.700
-And the process of it,
which is really cool.

00:04:27.700 --> 00:04:30.469
So, I think we had dinner
the Tuesday

00:04:30.469 --> 00:04:32.871
before the final
Christmas "SNL."

00:04:32.871 --> 00:04:34.673
-Yes, we went out to dinner.
-Yes.

00:04:34.673 --> 00:04:36.742
-Which, by the end of the week,
that seemed insane,

00:04:36.742 --> 00:04:38.511
because it was right
when omicron hit.

00:04:38.511 --> 00:04:42.148
-Yep. And it was like,
"Ha ha, we're so crazy

00:04:42.148 --> 00:04:43.316
for being out to dinner."
-Yeah.

00:04:43.316 --> 00:04:45.184
-And then, like, by Wednesday
it was like,

00:04:45.184 --> 00:04:47.920
"I can't [bleep]
believe we went out to dinner.

00:04:47.920 --> 00:04:50.089
Are we crazy?"
-"We have families!"

00:04:50.089 --> 00:04:53.458
-Yeah. But then -- And then
the crazy thing was you --

00:04:53.458 --> 00:04:55.795
So, Paul Rudd hosted
the Christmas episode of "SNL."

00:04:55.795 --> 00:04:58.897
And you showed up,
and that was crazy.

00:04:58.897 --> 00:05:00.399
-It was crazy.
That whole week was crazy.

00:05:00.399 --> 00:05:03.636
I think that week,
Thursday night, I went to do --

00:05:03.636 --> 00:05:06.171
I was a guest at the show
"Freestyle Love Supreme"

00:05:06.171 --> 00:05:07.406
on Broadway.
Did anyone get to see that?

00:05:07.406 --> 00:05:08.707
[ Cheers ]
It was very cool.

00:05:08.707 --> 00:05:11.743
So it was
a fully improvised rap.

00:05:11.743 --> 00:05:14.213
It's Lin-Manuel Miranda's show,

00:05:14.213 --> 00:05:16.382
and it's a fully improvised
rap musical.

00:05:16.382 --> 00:05:18.150
And they were like, "Will you
come and be a special guest?"

00:05:18.150 --> 00:05:20.286
And I used to be
a professional improviser.

00:05:20.286 --> 00:05:23.022
-Famously.
-I was in a union for it.

00:05:23.022 --> 00:05:24.489
-Right.

00:05:24.489 --> 00:05:26.191
-And I was like,
"I would love to."

00:05:26.191 --> 00:05:28.294
As it got closer, I started
to panic more and more.

00:05:28.294 --> 00:05:30.696
I was like, "They know that I
don't -- I don't improvise,

00:05:30.696 --> 00:05:32.598
like, raps at all, right?"

00:05:32.598 --> 00:05:34.000
I kept checking,
e-mailing people like,

00:05:34.000 --> 00:05:35.768
"But not music,
just like a story?"

00:05:35.768 --> 00:05:37.703
And they were like, "You're
going to have a great time."

00:05:37.703 --> 00:05:40.105
And I just -- As it got closer,
I got more and more nervous.

00:05:40.105 --> 00:05:43.910
The day of, I e-mailed with
the stage manager.

00:05:43.910 --> 00:05:47.479
I was like, "But not -- They
know I can't do music, right?"

00:05:47.479 --> 00:05:48.748
They were like,
"Sure, for sure."

00:05:48.748 --> 00:05:51.016
I got there,
and then also, like,

00:05:51.016 --> 00:05:52.318
everyone in the city had COVID.

00:05:52.318 --> 00:05:55.020
I was like, "Why am I in
a theater? This is nuts."

00:05:55.020 --> 00:05:57.723
Lin-Manuel Miranda was
in the show that night,

00:05:57.723 --> 00:05:59.759
I think because everyone else
had COVID.

00:05:59.759 --> 00:06:01.727
I'm not sure.
[ Laughter ]

00:06:01.727 --> 00:06:03.562
So I go with them,
and they're rehearsing me,

00:06:03.562 --> 00:06:05.631
and they were like, "Do you want
to play this game and this game?

00:06:05.631 --> 00:06:07.166
You would just have to,
like, sing the hook."

00:06:07.166 --> 00:06:11.237
And I was like, "I do not --"
Also I had looked up --

00:06:11.237 --> 00:06:13.138
I was like, "Who are the other
people who have been guests?"

00:06:13.138 --> 00:06:15.340
I looked it up, and it was like,
oh, Wayne Brady.

00:06:15.340 --> 00:06:17.110
That's not good.
That's not good.

00:06:17.110 --> 00:06:19.778
It was like, Jimmy [bleep]!

00:06:19.778 --> 00:06:21.280
Jimmy did this?

00:06:21.280 --> 00:06:23.783
So I was like,
"Nope, I can't sing the hook.

00:06:23.783 --> 00:06:25.584
I'll tell a story." And they
were really nice about it.

00:06:25.584 --> 00:06:27.686
And then seemed fine.

00:06:27.686 --> 00:06:29.788
Then we go to warm up
before the show.

00:06:29.788 --> 00:06:31.757
And they said, "We're gonna do,
like, an improv warm-up,

00:06:31.757 --> 00:06:33.993
if you want to come down."
So I go the basement.

00:06:33.993 --> 00:06:35.695
We're doing, like, regular
improv warm-ups.

00:06:35.695 --> 00:06:37.095
I'm like,
"Okay, we're in a circle."

00:06:37.095 --> 00:06:39.766
And then they start doing
their rap warm-up,

00:06:39.766 --> 00:06:42.268
which is they take words
out of a bucket

00:06:42.268 --> 00:06:45.837
and they freestyle rap,
and it's amazing.

00:06:45.837 --> 00:06:47.306
And they pass it to each other,

00:06:47.306 --> 00:06:49.542
and every single person
is amazing.

00:06:49.542 --> 00:06:50.977
And I'm in this circle.

00:06:50.977 --> 00:06:54.046
And I'm sweating from,
like, my spine out.

00:06:54.046 --> 00:06:56.281
And then they get to the person
next to me,

00:06:56.281 --> 00:06:58.150
and then I just,
like, lean back.

00:06:58.150 --> 00:07:01.220
And then that person just gives
it back to Lin-Manuel

00:07:01.220 --> 00:07:04.590
who, you know, does another one,

00:07:04.590 --> 00:07:06.893
and then, like,
tries to throw it to me.

00:07:06.893 --> 00:07:08.827
And I looked at
Lin-Manuel Miranda,

00:07:08.827 --> 00:07:12.031
and I went,
"No, I don't do that!"

00:07:12.031 --> 00:07:14.033
And then I threw myself
on the ground.

00:07:14.033 --> 00:07:15.701
[ Laughter ]

00:07:15.701 --> 00:07:17.436
And I was like,
"If anyone has taken improv,

00:07:17.436 --> 00:07:20.673
the only thing you're not
supposed to do is yell 'no.'"

00:07:20.673 --> 00:07:22.207
[ Laughter ]

00:07:22.207 --> 00:07:23.575
And I told Amy that story.
She was like,

00:07:23.575 --> 00:07:25.878
"Why didn't you just go like,
joop-de-beep-de-beep?"

00:07:25.878 --> 00:07:29.248
I was like, "I -- I panicked!"
[ Laughter ]

00:07:29.248 --> 00:07:31.350
But I just told a story,
and it was fine.

00:07:31.350 --> 00:07:33.752
-Alright, good.
-That's part one of the weekend.

00:07:33.752 --> 00:07:36.555
-Yeah.
-So then that's Thursday.

00:07:36.555 --> 00:07:39.859
I wake up Friday convinced
I have COVID. Right?

00:07:39.859 --> 00:07:41.961
I was with a full theater
of people.

00:07:41.961 --> 00:07:43.629
I'm supposed to shoot at
"Only Murders,"

00:07:43.629 --> 00:07:44.964
but they test you all the time.

00:07:44.964 --> 00:07:46.098
I'm like,
"Okay, my test is good."

00:07:46.098 --> 00:07:47.833
I go to
"Only Murders in the Building."

00:07:47.833 --> 00:07:51.370
I'm supposed to shoot with Marty
and Steve and then Selena Gomez.

00:07:51.370 --> 00:07:53.772
So I'm rehearsing with Marty.
You have your masks on.

00:07:53.772 --> 00:07:56.908
And they go -- And I'm like,
"Okay." [ Clears throat ]

00:07:56.908 --> 00:08:00.012
And then they go to put
the microphone on you,

00:08:00.012 --> 00:08:01.380
and then you're going to
take your mask off

00:08:01.380 --> 00:08:02.715
and they're gonna shoot,
and I was like,

00:08:02.715 --> 00:08:04.516
"Oh, my thr--

00:08:04.516 --> 00:08:05.985
My throat hurts a little bit."

00:08:05.985 --> 00:08:07.520
And I thought, you know,
I don't want to...

00:08:07.520 --> 00:08:09.287
-Yeah.

00:08:09.287 --> 00:08:11.757
-I'm not taking Marty and Steve
and Selena down, no way.

00:08:11.757 --> 00:08:15.795
So I pulled someone aside like,
"Can I have another rapid test?"

00:08:15.795 --> 00:08:18.630
And they're like,
"You know, we're just gonna, um,

00:08:18.630 --> 00:08:20.098
see what Disney says."

00:08:20.098 --> 00:08:22.067
And apparently what Disney says
was, "Get out of here."

00:08:22.067 --> 00:08:24.937
[ Laughter ]
So they sent me home.

00:08:24.937 --> 00:08:26.938
I should also -- Shoot, I messed
up the beginning of the story,

00:08:26.938 --> 00:08:29.375
is that I already knew on
Tuesday that I was supposed to

00:08:29.375 --> 00:08:31.210
go to "SNL" on Saturday.
-Yeah.

00:08:31.210 --> 00:08:34.814
-Because they needed someone
to do "Update" because...

00:08:34.814 --> 00:08:36.549
-Oh, right.
-...Jost was out.

00:08:36.549 --> 00:08:37.850
-Jost had COVID.
-Right.

00:08:37.850 --> 00:08:39.752
We can say that now, I guess.
-Yeah.

00:08:39.752 --> 00:08:41.921
[ Laughter ]

00:08:41.921 --> 00:08:43.122
-And so I was like, "Okay."

00:08:43.122 --> 00:08:44.624
So then they kick me out of
"Only Murders."

00:08:44.624 --> 00:08:46.158
I go home and I'm like --
[ Clears throat ]

00:08:46.158 --> 00:08:48.060
They give me another test.
Still good.

00:08:48.060 --> 00:08:50.262
I'm like, "Alright.
I'm going to do 'Update.'"

00:08:50.262 --> 00:08:52.598
I go to "SNL."
It's a ghost town.

00:08:52.598 --> 00:08:53.866
[ Laughter ]

00:08:53.866 --> 00:08:55.901
Everyone's there. Rudd is there.

00:08:55.901 --> 00:08:59.138
People are dropping like flies,
getting pulled, going home.

00:08:59.138 --> 00:09:02.675
And then somehow, that weird
show, it was just, like,

00:09:02.675 --> 00:09:08.213
me and Rudd and Kenan
and Che and Tom Hanks.

00:09:08.213 --> 00:09:11.684
Like, somehow, me and Tom Hanks
are the expendables.

00:09:11.684 --> 00:09:12.918
[ Laughter ]

00:09:12.918 --> 00:09:15.654
It was like, "No one cares
if these two die."

00:09:15.654 --> 00:09:18.957
And Tom Hanks is like,
"I had it. I had it first."

00:09:18.957 --> 00:09:20.759
-He had it first, yeah.
-Yeah.

00:09:20.759 --> 00:09:22.861
"I'm good."
-That was the thing.

